1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:01,500
What if every time someone thought about

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,990
you, you got one dollar?

3
00:00:02,990 --> 00:00:04,857
Not when they text you.

4
00:00:04,857 --> 00:00:06,850
Not when they like your post.

5
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:09,210
Just... when they think about you.

6
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,300
By the end of this week, you

7
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:12,575
would be a millionaire.

8
00:00:12,575 --> 00:00:14,320
And by the end of the month,

9
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:15,700
you would be begging for it to

10
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,300
stop.

11
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:18,040
Let's find out why.

12
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:19,700
It's Monday morning.

13
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:20,840
Your phone buzzes.

14
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,800
It's a notification from your bank.

15
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,940
Plus one dollar.

16
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,840
Then another. Plus one.

17
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:26,540
Plus one.

18
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:28,250
There's no name on the payment.

19
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:31,110
It just says: "Somebody thought of you."

20
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:32,670
You check the time.

21
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:34,800
It's six forty-two in the morning.

22
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,660
Downstairs, your mom is making breakfast, wondering

23
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:38,370
if you're going to be late again.

24
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:39,380
Plus one dollar.

25
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,200
At school, your best friend saves you

26
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,280
a seat. Plus one.

27
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:45,610
Your teacher looks at your empty homework

28
00:00:45,610 --> 00:00:47,270
folder. Plus one.

29
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:48,930
Actually... plus three.

30
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,440
By lunch, you've made eighteen dollars.

31
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:54,060
Not bad for doing absolutely nothing.

32
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:56,390
And then you notice something.

33
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,690
Your crush is sitting two tables away,

34
00:00:58,690 --> 00:01:00,470
laughing with their friends.

35
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:01,840
You look down at your phone.

36
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,430
Zero dollars. Ouch.

37
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:05,600
Then they glance your way.

38
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,830
Your phone buzzes.

39
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:08,530
Plus one dollar!

40
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:10,020
Your heart jumps.

41
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:10,900
And then you look down and see

42
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,190
the giant ketchup stain on your shirt.

43
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:14,520
Right. That's why.

44
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:16,860
So you start running tests.

45
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:18,490
Because if this is real, you need

46
00:01:18,490 --> 00:01:20,170
to know exactly how it works.

47
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:21,910
Rule number one.

48
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:23,160
It doesn't matter if the thought is

49
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,130
nice. When your little brother finds out

50
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:26,780
you ate the last of his cereal,

51
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:29,780
he's furious. Plus one dollar.

52
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:31,420
Plus one. Plus one.

53
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:32,430
You still get paid.

54
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:33,927
Rule number two.

55
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:36,280
It counts every single time.

56
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:38,220
If someone thinks about you ten times,

57
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,260
that's ten dollars.

58
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:41,620
Rule number three.

59
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,500
And this one is weird.

60
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,044
It works at night too.

61
00:01:44,044 --> 00:01:46,060
At two thirteen in the morning, your

62
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,390
phone lights up.

63
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:49,140
Plus one dollar.

64
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:51,840
Somebody, somewhere, is lying awake thinking about

65
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,440
you.

66
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:54,296
You decide not to ask who.

67
00:01:54,311 --> 00:01:55,708
Rule number four.

68
00:01:55,708 --> 00:01:57,570
You can't pay yourself.

69
00:01:57,570 --> 00:01:58,590
You stand in front of the mirror

70
00:01:58,590 --> 00:01:59,940
and think about yourself as hard as

71
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:01,530
you possibly can.

72
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:02,710
You think about how great your hair

73
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:05,400
looks. You think about your best qualities.

74
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,365
Nothing. Zero dollars.

75
00:02:07,365 --> 00:02:09,980
Apparently, the universe has rules against that.

76
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,960
By the end of day one, you've

77
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,720
made forty-seven dollars.

78
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:14,920
Most of it from your mom.

79
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,710
That night, you can't sleep.

80
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:18,450
So you build a tiny app.

81
00:02:18,450 --> 00:02:19,700
Every time a dollar comes in, it

82
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,440
puts a dot on a map, showing

83
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,860
where the thought came from.

84
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,790
Your house is covered in dots.

85
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:26,780
Your school has a few.

86
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:29,270
Your grandma's house, three hours away, has

87
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:31,590
one big glowing dot.

88
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,500
She thinks about you every night before

89
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,385
bed. You make a note to call

90
00:02:35,385 --> 00:02:36,220
her more often.

91
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,110
Now, let's do some math.

92
00:02:38,650 --> 00:02:40,540
A normal person is thought about maybe

93
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:42,360
fifty times a day.

94
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,890
Your family, your friends, your teachers, that

95
00:02:44,890 --> 00:02:47,072
one kid you bumped into in the

96
00:02:47,072 --> 00:02:49,370
hallway. That's fifty dollars a day.

97
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:51,910
About eighteen thousand dollars a year, just

98
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:52,510
for existing.

99
00:02:52,593 --> 00:02:54,600
But what about someone famous?

100
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,850
A popular YouTuber with ten million fans

101
00:02:57,850 --> 00:02:59,530
might be thought about millions of times

102
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:01,330
every single day.

103
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:02,750
That's millions of dollars.

104
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:04,800
Every. Single. Day.

105
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:07,460
And the biggest celebrities on Earth?

106
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,840
Hundreds of millions of thoughts.

107
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,350
They would become the richest people who

108
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:13,430
ever lived in less than a week.

109
00:03:13,457 --> 00:03:15,670
And here's the crazy part.

110
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:17,880
It wouldn't even stop when you die.

111
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,390
Think about Shakespeare.

112
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:21,700
Every year, millions of students are forced

113
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:23,810
to think about him in English class.

114
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:25,440
He'd still be getting paid.

115
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,710
Hundreds of years later.

116
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:28,760
And that's when it clicks.

117
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,830
The money isn't in being liked.

118
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:32,310
The money is in being noticed.

119
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:35,230
Tuesday. You make a plan.

120
00:03:35,270 --> 00:03:37,110
First, you try the easy stuff.

121
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:38,760
You dye your hair bright blue.

122
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,270
People stare all day.

123
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:41,380
Plus sixty dollars.

124
00:03:41,625 --> 00:03:43,488
Then you stand on a lunch table

125
00:03:43,488 --> 00:03:45,150
and sing the national anthem.

126
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:46,970
Loudly. And badly.

127
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:48,515
Plus three hundred dollars.

128
00:03:48,515 --> 00:03:50,910
And a week of detention.

129
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:52,350
Which means the principal is now thinking

130
00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:53,350
about you too.

131
00:03:53,350 --> 00:03:54,050
Plus one.

132
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,870
It's working. But it's not enough.

133
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:58,570
If you want real money, you need

134
00:03:58,570 --> 00:03:59,710
the whole internet.

135
00:03:59,935 --> 00:04:02,310
You film yourself doing the dumbest thing

136
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:03,520
you can think of.

137
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,360
You fill your entire bedroom with one

138
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,700
thousand rubber ducks.

139
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,690
Then you jump into them.

140
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:09,960
And you post it with a two-word

141
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,700
caption: "Why not?"

142
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:13,760
At first, nothing happens.

143
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,840
Twelve views. Plus twelve dollars.

144
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:18,190
Then a huge account shares it.

145
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:19,750
Plus one hundred.

146
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:20,930
Plus one thousand.

147
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:22,225
Plus ten thousand.

148
00:04:22,225 --> 00:04:23,770
Your phone gets so hot you have

149
00:04:23,770 --> 00:04:24,670
to put it in the fridge.

150
00:04:25,470 --> 00:04:27,510
By midnight, two million people have seen

151
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:28,700
the duck video.

152
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,290
And every single one of them thought

153
00:04:30,290 --> 00:04:31,630
about you for at least a second.

154
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,330
You go to bed with two million

155
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:35,990
dollars. You wake up with five.

156
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,410
Wednesday is a blur.

157
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,260
You pay off your parents' house.

158
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:41,580
You buy your best friend the gaming

159
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,420
computer they always wanted.

160
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:45,030
You order every pizza in town and

161
00:04:45,030 --> 00:04:46,790
give them away for free.

162
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:48,020
Which, by the way, makes the whole

163
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:49,560
town think about you.

164
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,190
More money.

165
00:04:50,370 --> 00:04:51,870
Then you try to buy a sports

166
00:04:51,870 --> 00:04:53,720
car. The salesman laughs.

167
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:56,970
You're fifteen. You can't even drive.

168
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:58,230
But you leave with a very nice

169
00:04:58,230 --> 00:05:00,280
golf cart, and the salesman thinks about

170
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,490
you for the rest of the day.

171
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:04,340
News reporters start showing up outside your

172
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:07,390
house. "Who is the duck kid?" Every

173
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,170
time the story airs, your phone vibrates

174
00:05:09,170 --> 00:05:09,780
like crazy.

175
00:05:10,690 --> 00:05:12,405
But then the bank calls.

176
00:05:12,405 --> 00:05:14,400
And calls again.

177
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,390
A teenager getting millions of dollars from

178
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:19,250
nowhere? That looks suspicious.

179
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:20,430
They freeze your account.

180
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:22,570
So you hire a lawyer.

181
00:05:22,570 --> 00:05:24,830
A very expensive lawyer, who can't stop

182
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:27,740
thinking about how strange your case is.

183
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:30,730
Plus one dollar, every few minutes.

184
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,760
Even your problems are paying you now.

185
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:34,560
And then Thursday happens.

186
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:37,540
Someone posts a video saying your duck

187
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,300
video was fake.

188
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:41,690
That you paid people to share it.

189
00:05:41,690 --> 00:05:43,050
Thousands of people get angry.

190
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:45,840
And here's the thing about angry people.

191
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:47,540
They think about you way more than

192
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:49,160
happy people do.

193
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:51,090
They think about you in the shower.

194
00:05:51,090 --> 00:05:52,310
They think about you while they type

195
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:55,120
mean comments. They think about you right

196
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,210
before they fall asleep.

197
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,490
Your money doesn't drop.

198
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:01,700
It explodes. Ten million dollars, in one

199
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,300
afternoon.

200
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:04,850
You open your thought map.

201
00:06:04,850 --> 00:06:06,450
Before, it was full of warm little

202
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:07,980
dots around your home.

203
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:10,150
Now the whole planet is glowing.

204
00:06:10,150 --> 00:06:12,240
Every city, every country.

205
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:14,830
Millions of people, all thinking about you

206
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:16,330
at the same time.

207
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:17,840
And almost none of them are thinking

208
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:18,650
anything nice.

209
00:06:19,660 --> 00:06:21,630
And now you face the hardest question

210
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:22,640
of your life.

211
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:25,330
If people hating you makes you richer...

212
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:26,230
would you let them?

213
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,530
At first, you say no.

214
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:29,430
Of course not.

215
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:32,010
But the numbers are right there, glowing

216
00:06:32,010 --> 00:06:32,780
on your screen.

217
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,890
And every time you do something annoying,

218
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:36,120
the counter spins faster.

219
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:39,700
So you start picking fights online.

220
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,570
You make reaction videos where you roast

221
00:06:41,570 --> 00:06:43,790
everyone. You become the person the whole

222
00:06:43,790 --> 00:06:45,030
internet loves to hate.

223
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:47,500
You start fake drama with a famous

224
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:50,450
singer. Her fans flood your comments.

225
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:52,480
Millions of angry messages.

226
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,540
Millions of dollars.

227
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,150
At school, people whisper when you walk

228
00:06:56,150 --> 00:06:58,740
by. Your little brother asks why everyone

229
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:01,210
is being mean about you online.

230
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:02,970
You tell him it's just a game.

231
00:07:02,970 --> 00:07:04,260
But he doesn't look convinced.

232
00:07:04,475 --> 00:07:06,080
And your mom?

233
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,750
She doesn't say anything.

234
00:07:07,750 --> 00:07:08,940
She just looks at you a little

235
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:10,020
differently at dinner.

236
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:12,400
By Friday, you are a billionaire.

237
00:07:12,715 --> 00:07:15,270
And by Friday, your best friend has

238
00:07:15,270 --> 00:07:16,540
stopped answering your texts.

239
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:19,130
Here's what nobody tells you about being

240
00:07:19,130 --> 00:07:20,710
famous on the internet.

241
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:22,270
People move on.

242
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:22,870
Fast.

243
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,410
Saturday morning, somebody else goes viral.

244
00:07:25,410 --> 00:07:26,910
A guy who taught his cat to

245
00:07:26,910 --> 00:07:28,440
play the drums.

246
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,550
And just like that, the whole world

247
00:07:30,550 --> 00:07:31,670
forgets about you.

248
00:07:32,150 --> 00:07:33,760
Ten million thoughts a day becomes one

249
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:36,340
million. Then a hundred thousand.

250
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:37,250
Then almost nothing.

251
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,390
You still have the money.

252
00:07:39,390 --> 00:07:41,210
But your phone goes quiet.

253
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:42,810
And for the first time all week,

254
00:07:42,810 --> 00:07:44,390
nobody is thinking about you.

255
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,160
So you panic.

256
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,730
You try to win them back.

257
00:07:47,730 --> 00:07:49,370
You fill your house with ten thousand

258
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:51,020
rubber ducks this time.

259
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:53,550
Forty views. You try another fight with

260
00:07:53,550 --> 00:07:55,360
the singer. She doesn't even reply.

261
00:07:56,370 --> 00:07:57,820
You stare at the counter for hours,

262
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,450
waiting for it to move.

263
00:07:59,450 --> 00:08:02,120
It's the loneliest feeling in the world.

264
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,600
Not because you're poor.

265
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,590
Because nobody's thinking about you anymore.

266
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:08,840
Except... at six forty-two in the morning,

267
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,180
your phone buzzes.

268
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,260
Plus one dollar.

269
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:12,730
It's your mom.

270
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:14,090
She's wondering if you've had breakfast.

271
00:08:15,110 --> 00:08:16,910
Sunday. You sit on the floor of

272
00:08:16,910 --> 00:08:19,160
your huge, empty new house.

273
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:21,240
The counter says one point two billion

274
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:21,840
dollars.

275
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:25,300
And you realize the strangest thing.

276
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:27,170
The billions from strangers felt like nothing.

277
00:08:27,170 --> 00:08:29,620
But that one dollar from your mom,

278
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:31,390
every single morning?

279
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:32,620
That's the one that made you smile.

280
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,000
So you decide to do something different

281
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,540
with all that money.

282
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:37,830
You build a new library at your

283
00:08:37,830 --> 00:08:40,230
school. You pay for your teacher's dream

284
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:42,700
trip. You send your grandma flowers every

285
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:43,500
single week.

286
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:47,000
And slowly, something changes.

287
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,820
The thoughts start coming back.

288
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,200
Not millions of them.

289
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,630
Just a few.

290
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:54,110
But this time, they're warm.

291
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:55,663
People aren't thinking about the duck kid,

292
00:08:55,663 --> 00:08:56,980
or the villain.

293
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,130
They're thinking about you.

294
00:08:58,024 --> 00:09:00,440
So you call your best friend.

295
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,240
You say sorry.

296
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,700
And after a long pause, they say:

297
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:05,380
"It's okay. Honestly...

298
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:07,020
I've been thinking about you all week."

299
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:08,950
Your phone buzzes.

300
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:10,020
Plus one dollar.

301
00:09:10,890 --> 00:09:12,350
Some people are worth billions.

302
00:09:12,350 --> 00:09:14,230
But some thoughts are worth more than

303
00:09:14,230 --> 00:09:14,830
money.

304
00:09:15,090 --> 00:09:16,550
So now I'm curious.

305
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:17,923
How much money would you have made

306
00:09:17,923 --> 00:09:19,950
today? And who do you think is

307
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:22,080
thinking about you right now?

308
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,340
Maybe it's your mom.

309
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:25,070
Maybe it's your best friend.

310
00:09:25,070 --> 00:09:26,350
Maybe it's someone you haven't talked to

311
00:09:26,350 --> 00:09:26,950
in years.

312
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,630
Here's a challenge.

313
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:30,040
Send a message to the person you

314
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,660
think about the most.

315
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:33,000
Just one text.

316
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,290
Because somewhere, right now, your phone could

317
00:09:35,290 --> 00:09:36,833
be about to buzz.

318
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:37,653
Tell me in the comments.

319
00:09:37,653 --> 00:09:40,610
And if you enjoyed this, subscribe.

320
00:09:40,610 --> 00:09:42,590
Because somebody out there is definitely thinking

321
00:09:42,590 --> 00:09:43,300
about you.
